00:48:44.570 --> 00:48:50.750
Well, we had a fan question in this scene from Tennille, who wants to know, in this episode,
嗯，我们在这个场景里收到一个粉丝提问，来自坦尼尔，她想知道，在这一集里，

848
00:48:50.970 --> 00:48:54.990
there are a lot of talking heads with Michael facing the window where it's snowing.
有很多迈克尔面对窗户的访谈镜头，窗外正在下雪。

849
00:48:55.190 --> 00:49:00.870
Were those talking heads shot in sequence so that they didn't have to keep turning the snow on and off?
这些访谈镜头是连续拍摄的吗，这样他们就不用反复开关造雪机了？

850
00:49:00.870 --> 00:49:04.070
Well, yes, yes.
嗯，是的，没错。

851
00:49:04.070 --> 00:49:07.530
I love this question, Angela, because we've never really talked about this.
安吉拉，我很喜欢这个问题，因为我们真的从来没聊过这个。

852
00:49:07.670 --> 00:49:11.710
We always shot all of our talking heads in a row.
我们所有的“访谈”镜头都是集中拍摄的。

853
00:49:12.150 --> 00:49:17.930
So what they would do is they would set up the shot, let's say, in Michael's office for a talking head.
他们会先布置好机位，比如在迈克尔的办公室里拍访谈。

854
00:49:18.050 --> 00:49:24.070
And every talking head he had for that episode, they would spend hours doing all of them.
那一集里他所有的访谈镜头，他们会花上几个小时一次性拍完。

855
00:49:24.070 --> 00:49:25.990
And the same thing in the conference room.
会议室里也是一样。

856
00:49:26.170 --> 00:49:32.270
Remember, they'd set up the chair and we would all cycle in for hours and do our talking heads.
记得吗？他们会摆好椅子，我们所有人轮流进去，花上几个小时拍完各自的访谈。

857
00:49:32.690 --> 00:49:35.610
Yes, it would literally be like talking head day on set.
没错，片场简直就像是“访谈日”一样。

858
00:49:36.190 --> 00:49:39.870
And I always really felt for Steve because he always had the moSt.
我一直很同情史蒂夫，因为他的访谈镜头最多。

859
00:49:40.110 --> 00:49:46.710
And I would think like, oh, my God, I had to like learn one, you know, and maybe they would give me some alts on the day.
我会想，天哪，我只要背好一段台词就行，而且他们当天可能还会给我一些备选方案。

860
00:49:47.170 --> 00:49:51.090
But Steve had to learn so many and just sit there and do them and do them.
但史蒂夫要背那么多台词，还得坐在那儿一遍又一遍地拍。

861
00:49:51.090 --> 00:49:57.770
And Veda would be there, our script supervisor, and sometimes she would remind you if you had more than one.
我们的场记维达会在旁边，有时候如果你有不止一段访谈，她会提醒你。

862
00:49:57.890 --> 00:50:03.890
Okay, now remember, this talking head is after Dwight left, so you're more sad than the one before, you know?
比如，“记住，这段访谈是在德怀特离开之后拍的，所以你要比上一段看起来更难过一点，明白吗？”

863
00:50:04.070 --> 00:50:07.610
So sometimes she was helping us kind of navigate the time sequence of it all.
所以有时候她会帮我们理清这些镜头的时间顺序。

864
00:50:08.410 --> 00:50:08.690
Yes.
是的。

865
00:50:09.090 --> 00:50:15.370
And we would usually do these either first thing in the morning or at the end of the day.
我们通常会在清晨或者一天结束时拍这些镜头。

866
00:50:15.630 --> 00:50:17.390
Steve would always do his first thing in the morning.
史蒂夫总是会在清晨先拍完他的部分。

867
00:50:17.390 --> 00:50:19.070
I think he liked to lead with them.
我想他喜欢先搞定这些。

868
00:50:19.310 --> 00:50:25.790
He would oftentimes, I feel like on a Monday, it would be like Steve talking heads until almost lunch.
我感觉通常在周一，史蒂夫几乎一上午都在拍访谈。

869
00:50:25.970 --> 00:50:26.330
Yeah.
没错。

870
00:50:26.470 --> 00:50:30.790
And then we would all come in and film like group scenes for the rest of the day.
然后我们其他人会进来，拍剩下的群戏。

871
00:50:31.050 --> 00:50:31.230
Yeah.
是啊。

872
00:50:31.830 --> 00:50:38.570
But then on Fridays, we would spend Friday afternoons all the rest of the cast doing our talking heads.
但到了周五下午，剩下的演员会花时间拍各自的访谈。

873
00:50:38.770 --> 00:50:40.670
That was kind of how we framed our week.
这就是我们安排一周工作的方式。

874
00:50:40.950 --> 00:50:42.330
Yeah, that's how I remember it too.
没错，我也记得是这样。

875
00:50:42.330 --> 00:50:47.370
Well, Jenna, you know, Oscar's back now and he walks back over to accounting.
珍娜，奥斯卡现在回来了，他走回了会计部。

876
00:50:47.750 --> 00:50:51.950
And of course, Kevin has a ridiculous joke that he's been saving for weeks.
当然，凯文有个荒唐的笑话已经憋了好几周了。

877
00:50:52.190 --> 00:50:53.070
Kevin thought of it.
那是凯文想出来的。

878
00:50:53.190 --> 00:50:54.330
He was like, how was your gaycation?
他说：“你的‘同性假期’（gaycation）过得怎么样？”

879
00:50:54.590 --> 00:50:55.410
Oscar's like, awesome.
奥斯卡说：“棒极了。”

880
00:50:55.990 --> 00:50:57.230
Kevin's like, yeah, I thought of that.
凯文说：“是啊，我想出来的。”

881
00:50:57.430 --> 00:50:58.790
Two seconds after you left.
“就在你走后两秒钟。”

882
00:50:59.110 --> 00:51:00.510
Kevin's so proud of himself.
凯文对自己得意极了。

883
00:51:01.910 --> 00:51:03.870
And Angela is just like, hello.
而安吉拉只是说了声：“你好。”

884
00:51:04.110 --> 00:51:04.950
And he's like, hello.
他也回了句：“你好。”

885
00:51:04.950 --> 00:51:11.610
And you can tell that there's, I feel like a lot she wants to say, but she's not, she's not ready yet.
你能感觉到，我觉得她有很多话想说，但她还没准备好。

886
00:51:11.870 --> 00:51:13.010
She doesn't know how to say it yet.
她还不知道该怎么开口。

887
00:51:13.570 --> 00:51:13.790
Yeah.
是啊。

888
00:51:14.070 --> 00:51:19.790
But then eventually, Angela does invite Oscar to join the party planning committee.
但最终，安吉拉还是邀请了奥斯卡加入派对策划委员会。

889
00:51:20.010 --> 00:51:27.150
She says she's sorry for the way certain things transpired and she wants to make some changes and she starts crying.
她说她对某些事情的发生方式感到抱歉，她想做出一些改变，然后她开始哭了。

890
00:51:27.830 --> 00:51:27.970
Yeah.
没错。

891
00:51:29.030 --> 00:51:30.870
Well, Jenna, I really cried.
珍娜，我是真的哭了。

892
00:51:31.050 --> 00:51:32.610
That was me really crying.
那是我真情流露的哭戏。

893
00:51:32.970 --> 00:51:38.010
And I had a whole conversation with Greg about it as we were trying to find the scene.
在打磨这场戏的时候，我和格雷格进行了深入的交流。

894
00:51:38.250 --> 00:51:43.290
And I did one take and he was like, Angela, I'm feeling sad.
我拍了一遍，他说：“安吉拉，我感到很难过。”

895
00:51:43.290 --> 00:51:45.850
And he said, this has to be a funny cry.
他说，这必须是一种“好笑的哭”。

896
00:51:46.790 --> 00:51:50.830
Where sometimes on a show, someone cries and it breaks your heart.
有时候在剧里，有人哭会让人心碎。

897
00:51:50.990 --> 00:51:53.510
He said, this needs to be just awkward.
他说，这段哭戏必须显得很尴尬。

898
00:51:54.310 --> 00:51:59.830
Like, and then at the end, we have a joke because Kevin says, can I join?
最后我们还有个笑话，因为凯文问：“我能加入吗？”

899
00:51:59.950 --> 00:52:00.690
And I say, never.
我说：“休想。”

900
00:52:01.090 --> 00:52:01.510
Right.
没错。

901
00:52:02.370 --> 00:52:10.590
So, so it was sort of this interesting thing of figuring out how do you cry, but you don't make people feel bad, you know?
所以，这其实是一件挺有意思的事，得琢磨怎么哭才能不让观众觉得难受，你懂吗？

902
00:52:10.990 --> 00:52:15.430
So, so, and what really helped me was that my lines were so ridiculous.
所以，真正帮到我的是我的台词太荒谬了。

903
00:52:15.530 --> 00:52:21.890
So it was, you know, me being like certain events transpired and certain people said certain things.
所以就是，你知道，我表现得像是发生了某些事，某些人说了某些话。

904
00:52:22.110 --> 00:52:22.890
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

905
00:52:22.890 --> 00:52:23.690
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

906
00:52:23.890 --> 00:52:29.830
But it was sort of this art for my character to find a way to cry that was just more awkward than sad.
但对我这个角色来说，找到一种比悲伤更尴尬的哭法，这算是一种艺术。

907
00:52:30.350 --> 00:52:32.690
Well, you just made someone very happy.
好吧，你刚刚让某人非常开心。

908
00:52:33.890 --> 00:52:40.550
Sarah Cooper had written in to ask you, did you have to do anything different to get into character in preparation for this episode?
莎拉·库珀来信问你，为了准备这一集，你是否需要做些特别的准备来进入角色？

909
00:52:40.790 --> 00:52:45.130
You know, when you cry, we all have a little bit of our process of actors of how we get to that place.
你知道，当你要哭的时候，我们演员都有自己的一套方法来进入那种状态。

910
00:52:45.130 --> 00:52:51.630
But it was this sort of interesting thing to get myself there, but then kind of pull back a little bit.
但要让自己进入那种状态，然后再稍微收敛一点，这确实挺有意思的。

911
00:52:51.770 --> 00:52:57.030
And this might be really boring, actor-y stuff, but it was a really interesting exercise.
这可能听起来很无聊，全是演员那一套，但这确实是一个非常有趣的练习。

912
00:52:57.030 --> 00:53:00.530
Well, we had another fan question, Angela, from Beatrix Smith.
好吧，安吉拉，我们还有另一个粉丝比阿特丽克斯·史密斯的问题。

913
00:53:01.050 --> 00:53:03.450
Was it weird for you to have Oscar back?
奥斯卡回来对你来说奇怪吗？

914
00:53:03.710 --> 00:53:05.310
Did you miss him when he was gone?
他不在的时候你有没有想他？

915
00:53:05.530 --> 00:53:06.010
Oh, yeah.
哦，当然。

916
00:53:06.190 --> 00:53:08.190
I think Angela definitely missed Oscar.
我觉得安吉拉绝对想念奥斯卡。

917
00:53:08.350 --> 00:53:14.690
Listen, him being gone means, A, she's carrying most of the workload in accounting because Kevin's no help, really.
听着，他不在意味着，第一，会计部大部分工作都得她来扛，因为凯文根本帮不上忙。

918
00:53:15.190 --> 00:53:22.710
And I think that Oscar and Angela really are these sort of mismatched roommates, if you will.
而且我觉得奥斯卡和安吉拉就像是一对不怎么合拍的室友，如果你愿意这么说的话。

919
00:53:22.870 --> 00:53:26.210
And you'll see their friendship come through throughout the seasons.
你会看到他们的友谊在后续几季中逐渐显现。

920
00:53:26.210 --> 00:53:28.850
But they are there for each other.
但他们确实会互相支持。

921
00:53:29.030 --> 00:53:32.810
It's just, I think they just had some hurdles to get over.
只是我觉得他们之间有一些障碍需要克服。

922
00:53:34.090 --> 00:53:35.630
Oh, well, that's a nice answer.
哦，那真是个不错的回答。

923
00:53:35.790 --> 00:53:37.310
I think she meant you, Angela.
我想她指的是你，安吉拉。

924
00:53:37.690 --> 00:53:38.170
Oh!
哦！

925
00:53:38.290 --> 00:53:41.030
Did you miss your friend, Oscar, who hadn't been sitting there with you?
你有没有想念你的朋友奥斯卡，那个没坐在你身边的人？

926
00:53:41.670 --> 00:53:46.230
But I like how you stayed in character there for that answer.
但我喜欢你刚才回答时保持角色状态的样子。

927
00:53:46.610 --> 00:53:49.270
Well, we were talking so much about Angela Martin.
好吧，我们刚才一直在谈论安吉拉·马丁。

928
00:53:50.470 --> 00:53:52.430
Well, of course I missed my friend.
好吧，我当然想念我的朋友了。

929
00:53:52.430 --> 00:53:53.150
Are you kidding?
开什么玩笑？

930
00:53:53.450 --> 00:53:59.250
I didn't have anyone to draw me little crazy cartoons of myself being silly and passing me notes.
我都没人给我画那些关于我自己的疯狂小漫画，也没人给我传纸条了。

931
00:53:59.530 --> 00:54:01.930
You guys are such a little trio over there.
你们在那边真是个铁三角。

932
00:54:02.210 --> 00:54:04.190
Yeah, I definitely missed him.
是啊，我绝对想他了。

933
00:54:04.530 --> 00:54:08.230
Well, while all of this is going on, Andy is just stalking Michael.
好吧，在这一切发生的同时，安迪一直在跟踪迈克尔。

934
00:54:08.770 --> 00:54:12.950
Yeah, he's like looking for him everywhere and he follows him to the bathroom.
是啊，他到处找他，甚至跟着他进了洗手间。

935
00:54:13.330 --> 00:54:13.550
Yeah.
没错。

936
00:54:14.070 --> 00:54:17.310
Jenna, Andy now has two expressions that I love.
珍娜，安迪现在有两个我超爱的口头禅。

937
00:54:17.470 --> 00:54:20.430
We first heard nifty gifties from Andy.
我们第一次从安迪那听到的是“精巧礼物”。

938
00:54:21.050 --> 00:54:22.630
Love me the nifty gifties.
我超爱“精巧礼物”这个词。

939
00:54:22.770 --> 00:54:24.850
And in this one, Michael's like, what's up?
在这一集里，迈克尔问他，怎么了？

940
00:54:25.010 --> 00:54:26.410
And Andy goes, nerfin.
安迪回答说，没啥（nerfin）。

941
00:54:28.090 --> 00:54:28.570
Nerfin.
没啥。

942
00:54:29.010 --> 00:54:29.490
Nerfin.
没啥。

943
00:54:29.810 --> 00:54:33.570
Me and my kids are saying nerfin.
我和我的孩子们现在都在说“没啥”。

944
00:54:33.850 --> 00:54:36.350
It just, it has stuck here at the house.
它在我们家已经成了口头禅了。

945
00:54:36.490 --> 00:54:37.650
I thought it was so funny.
我觉得这太搞笑了。

946
00:54:37.650 --> 00:54:43.590
But yeah, Andy's driving Michael crazy and Michael has a whole talking head from behind
但确实，安迪快把迈克尔逼疯了，迈克尔甚至躲在门后录了一段采访。

947
00:54:43.590 --> 00:54:44.170
his door.
他在躲着。

948
00:54:44.370 --> 00:54:45.030
He's hiding.
他在躲着。

949
00:54:45.870 --> 00:54:51.750
It was, it made me laugh out loud because I didn't know where he was during this because
这让我大笑出声，因为我不知道他当时在哪，因为

950
00:54:51.750 --> 00:54:53.890
Andy's looking for him and he's just nowhere.
安迪到处找他，但他根本就不在。

951
00:54:53.890 --> 00:54:54.810
He's nowhere.
他哪儿也不在。

952
00:54:55.270 --> 00:54:59.770
And then when he's revealed to be giving this whole talking head from behind his door,
然后当他被发现躲在门后接受采访时，

953
00:54:59.990 --> 00:55:05.350
one of the things I loved about it most was that while hiding, he was still compelled
我最喜欢的一点是，即使在躲藏的时候，他还是忍不住

954
00:55:05.350 --> 00:55:07.410
to perform and speak to the camera.
要对着镜头表演和说话。

955
00:55:08.210 --> 00:55:15.350
He was like, I'm hiding, but I'm not going to stop presenting myself to this camera crew.
他就像是说，我在躲着，但我不会停止在摄制组面前表现自己。

956
00:55:15.770 --> 00:55:19.930
I wonder if he was like, I'm going to hide and you have to too, because if Andy sees you
我在想他当时是不是说，我要躲起来，你们也得躲，因为如果安迪看到你们

957
00:55:19.930 --> 00:55:24.170
guys in here, so like, is there a room where the camera crew is like smushed up against
在这儿，所以，是不是有个房间，摄制组的人都挤在

958
00:55:24.170 --> 00:55:25.850
the wall, also hiding?
墙边，也在躲着？

959
00:55:26.750 --> 00:55:28.070
That's such a good point.
这话说得太对了。

960
00:55:28.250 --> 00:55:31.530
Like all Andy has to look for is like, where's the camera pointed?
安迪只需要看看镜头对着哪儿就行了，对吧？

961
00:55:31.810 --> 00:55:32.010
Yeah.
没错。

962
00:55:32.630 --> 00:55:35.230
There's a crew constantly following Michael around.
有个摄制组一直在跟着迈克尔。

963
00:55:35.230 --> 00:55:40.990
Well, we're coming up on a scene that completely destroyed John Krasinski in real life.
嗯，我们接下来要讲的这一幕，在现实生活中彻底让约翰·卡拉辛斯基笑崩了。

964
00:55:41.170 --> 00:55:45.290
I don't think he's ever laughed so hard ever, ever on the show.
我觉得他在剧里从来没笑得这么厉害过。

965
00:55:45.510 --> 00:55:48.210
He has said it's the hardest he laughed the whole series.
他说这是他整部剧里笑得最厉害的一次。

966
00:55:48.530 --> 00:55:50.630
Like, and I texted Creed about it.
我为此还给克里德发了短信。

967
00:55:50.890 --> 00:55:51.170
Yeah.
是啊。

968
00:55:51.350 --> 00:55:55.750
It's this scene in the kitchen where Oscar comes in and he's just kind of like, where's
就是厨房里的那一幕，奥斯卡走进来，他大概是问，

969
00:55:55.750 --> 00:55:56.310
Dwight?
德怀特在哪儿？

970
00:55:56.650 --> 00:56:05.750
And Creed says Dwight was decapitated and they had a funeral for a bird, which is not
然后克里德说德怀特被斩首了，他们还给一只鸟办了葬礼，这根本

971
00:56:05.750 --> 00:56:06.230
correct.
不对。

972
00:56:06.470 --> 00:56:07.830
But kind of correct.
但又有点对。

973
00:56:08.110 --> 00:56:10.090
Just all mushed up together.
就是把所有事都混在一起了。

974
00:56:10.450 --> 00:56:10.990
Yeah.
没错。

975
00:56:11.190 --> 00:56:14.970
Ed Truck was decapitated and they did have a funeral for a bird.
是埃德·卡车被斩首了，而且他们确实给一只鸟办了葬礼。

976
00:56:15.110 --> 00:56:17.850
And remember, Jim wasn't around for any of this.
记住，吉姆当时根本不在场。

977
00:56:18.030 --> 00:56:21.530
So Jim isn't even able to like correct this.
所以吉姆甚至都没法纠正这一点。

978
00:56:21.530 --> 00:56:25.130
So he just says, I'm pretty sure that's not real.
于是他只是说，我确定那不是真的。

979
00:56:25.490 --> 00:56:28.730
And then Creed says, you're not real, man.
然后克里德说，你才不是真的，伙计。

980
00:56:29.890 --> 00:56:33.450
And that is the line that destroyed John Krasinski.
就是这句台词让约翰·卡拉辛斯基彻底笑崩了。

981
00:56:33.970 --> 00:56:34.130
Yeah.
是啊。

982
00:56:34.630 --> 00:56:37.070
John could not keep it together.
约翰根本控制不住自己。

983
00:56:37.370 --> 00:56:40.330
He crumbled like into just bits of laughter.
他笑得整个人都瘫了。

984
00:56:40.330 --> 00:56:42.010
And I texted Creed.
我给克里德发了短信。

985
00:56:42.150 --> 00:56:44.990
I was like, Creed, oh, my gosh, we're breaking down the return.
我说，克里德，天哪，我们正在解析《回归》这一集。

